=== cell 8
==============================================================================
  tokens                                   (8, 128)     B=batch of independent char windows, T=position in the window
  wte(tokens)+wpe(pos)  hidden             (8, 128, 128) B, T as above, C=embedding width (n_embd)
  lm_head.weight  (tied to wte.weight)     (65, 128)    V=one row per character, C as above; z = h @ W^T, same tensor as the input embedding
  logits                                   (8, 128, 65) B, T as above, V=one score per character
  logits.grad                              (8, 128, 65) same shape as logits — one gradient per (batch, position, character) score
  lm_head.weight.grad                      (65, 128)    same shape as lm_head.weight — because of tying, this IS wte.weight.grad too
  wte.weight.grad is lm_head.weight.grad   True         tying means one gradient tensor serves both roles, not two equal ones
  blocks[0].attn.c_attn.weight.grad        (384, 128)   [3C, C] — packed Q,K,V projection, gradient matches the weight

